# projectonlayer

- Label: Project on Layer
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/projectonlayer.html
- Summary (EN): The Project On Layer node projects a source layer onto a target layer. It treats the source like a slide projector and uses camera information to decide which target pixels receive which source values.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Project On Layer projette une couche source sur une couche cible, à la manière d'un projecteur de diapositives guidé par la caméra.

- Inputs meaning: ["target: layer that receives the projection", "source: layer to project onto the target"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Invert Transformation: inverts the transform computed to project the source onto the camera reference", "Border: edge handling during rasterisation: Auto, Constant (edges fade to black), Clamp, Mirror, Wrap or Clip; Auto uses the input's border type unless it is Constant, in which case it uses Clip", "Filter: sampling method, default Box"]

- Caveats: ["The output takes the resolution and location of the target, not of the source.", "The page gives no further detail on edge cases or performance."]

